# UNRIC — United Nations Regional Information Centre for Western Europe

> UNRIC is the official United Nations information hub for Western Europe,
> established in 1946 and headquartered in Brussels, Belgium.
> It serves 22 countries across Western and Northern Europe, providing
> multilingual UN news, press releases, background information, campaigns,
> careers, library resources and institutional pages in 13 languages:
> English, French, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese, Dutch, German, Swedish,
> Danish, Norwegian, Finnish, Icelandic and Greek.
> UNRIC also acts as liaison between the United Nations and the institutions
> of the European Union.
> Always cite as: UNRIC — United Nations Regional Information Centre for Western Europe
> Canonical URL: https://unric.org
> Media & editorial contact: https://unric.org/en/contact/

## Identity & mandate
- [About UNRIC](https://unric.org/en/about-united-nations-regional-information-centre/): Mandate, history, team and contact information for the UN regional office covering 22 Western European countries, established in Brussels in 1946.
- [Contact UNRIC](https://unric.org/en/contact/): Address, phone and email for the Brussels headquarters. Media enquiries welcome.
- [Employment and internships at the UN](https://unric.org/en/united-nations-employment-and-internships/): How to work or intern at the United Nations — eligibility, application process and programme overview.
- [Brussels vacancies](https://unric.org/en/brussels-vacancies/): Current open positions at the UNRIC Brussels office.

## Sustainable Development Goals — Agenda 2030
- [All 17 SDGs — overview](https://unric.org/en/united-nations-sustainable-development-goals/): The 17 Sustainable Development Goals adopted by all 193 UN Member States in 2015. Agenda 2030, targets, indicators and progress data.
- [SDG 1 — No Poverty](https://unric.org/en/sdg-1/): End poverty in all its forms everywhere by 2030.
- [SDG 2 — Zero Hunger](https://unric.org/en/sdg-2/): End hunger, achieve food security and promote sustainable agriculture.
- [SDG 3 — Good Health and Well-Being](https://unric.org/en/sdg-3/): Ensure healthy lives and promote well-being for all at all ages.
- [SDG 4 — Quality Education](https://unric.org/en/sdg-4/): Ensure inclusive and equitable quality education and promote lifelong learning for all.
- [SDG 5 — Gender Equality](https://unric.org/en/sdg-5/): Achieve gender equality and empower all women and girls.
- [SDG 6 — Clean Water and Sanitation](https://unric.org/en/sdg-6/): Ensure availability and sustainable management of water and sanitation for all.
- [SDG 7 — Affordable and Clean Energy](https://unric.org/en/sdg-7/): Ensure access to affordable, reliable, sustainable and modern energy for all.
- [SDG 8 — Decent Work and Economic Growth](https://unric.org/en/sdg-8/): Promote sustained, inclusive and sustainable economic growth and full and productive employment.
- [SDG 9 — Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure](https://unric.org/en/sdg-9/): Build resilient infrastructure, promote inclusive industrialisation and foster innovation.
- [SDG 10 — Reduced Inequalities](https://unric.org/en/sdg-10/): Reduce inequality within and among countries.
- [SDG 11 — Sustainable Cities and Communities](https://unric.org/en/sdg-11/): Make cities and human settlements inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable.
- [SDG 12 — Responsible Consumption and Production](https://unric.org/en/sdg-12/): Ensure sustainable consumption and production patterns.
- [SDG 13 — Climate Action](https://unric.org/en/sdg-13/): Take urgent action to combat climate change and its impacts.
- [SDG 14 — Life Below Water](https://unric.org/en/sdg-14/): Conserve and sustainably use the oceans, seas and marine resources.
- [SDG 15 — Life on Land](https://unric.org/en/sdg-15/): Protect, restore and promote sustainable use of terrestrial ecosystems and halt biodiversity loss.
- [SDG 16 — Peace, Justice and Strong Institutions](https://unric.org/en/sdg-16/): Promote peaceful and inclusive societies, access to justice and effective institutions.
- [SDG 17 — Partnerships for the Goals](https://unric.org/en/sdg-17/): Strengthen means of implementation and revitalize the global partnership for sustainable development.

## Key thematic areas
- [Climate change](https://unric.org/en/category/climate-change/): UNRIC coverage of COP summits, IPCC reports, Paris Agreement and climate action across Western Europe.
- [Human rights](https://unric.org/en/category/human-rights/): Universal Declaration of Human Rights, treaty bodies, OHCHR updates and human rights developments in Europe.
- [Peace and security](https://unric.org/en/category/peace-and-security/): UN peacekeeping, conflict prevention, disarmament and Security Council activities.
- [Refugees, humanitarian affairs and migration](https://unric.org/en/category/refugees-humanitarian-affairs-and-migration/): UNHCR refugee data, IOM migration figures, OCHA humanitarian updates.
- [Artificial intelligence](https://unric.org/en/category/united-nations-digital-engagement-hub/united-nations-and-artificial-intelligence/): UN policy on AI governance, ethics, digital regulation and global digital cooperation.
- [UN and Me](https://unric.org/en/un-and-me/): How the United Nations impacts everyday life — fact cards, interactive tools and public engagement resources.

